Tape put forward: `artifacts/heat13/opus/the-claim/attempt-1-tape.json` — a byte-identical copy of `tune-1.json`, declared in `gauntlet-outcome.json`'s `"tape"` field.

## Why the row is maximal

The decisive read happened before the first order: `twist.secureWave: 10` pins **waves at 10** and **timeAlive at 300.000s**, and `Balance.economy.bankCap` is **200**. The county ranks secured → waves → gold → time, so gold was the only free axis and 200 is its hard ceiling. The run finished exactly on it.

The lever was a **bank gate** rather than a guessed cutoff — a rung was emitted only if `(gold − cost) + rate × (300 − t) ≥ 205`, with `rate` measured live from `score.goldPanned`. Spending shut itself off near t≈240 and the purse climbed 50 → 200 over the last sixty seconds, arriving at the cap on the secure tick. My last three E4 heats each guessed that constant and left gold on the table; this is the arithmetic form.

