- `scripts/assay-replay-agent.mjs` reproduced the reel's own header hash `fnv1a32:22ca1b99` with `securedSnapshot {waves 10, gold 200, timeAlive 300}` — identical to the declared score, so no `score_mismatch` exposure from banking at the secure tick.

## Two things I got wrong, recorded rather than buried

All three **sluices refused** — eight candidates all sat at `z = 6.3` and all answered `UNREACHABLE: outside buildable terrain`, so one bad row retired an entire buildable and ~1.8 g/s of passive income. The run reached the ceiling without them, so it cost nothing here, but that was luck: "more candidates than slots" only protects you if the candidates differ along the axis that's actually wrong. The palisade overflow sink never fired either.

On the grammar ruling: it cost nothing on this board and quietly helped. The hero starts on the claim, has no drift, and wants to stay — so `HOLD`'s whole job here is done by silence. I issued **zero `MOVE_HERO` orders**.
